-- title:
--   Frobenius kernel lies in the Verschiebung image on G[p]
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $k$ a field of characteristic $p$, $h$ a natural number, and let $G$ be a $p$-divisible group over $k$ of height $h$ in the sense of the structure [`PDivisibleGroup`](def/PDivisibleGroup_Basic.html#L199): a family of types $A_v =$ `G.level v` ($v \in \mathbb{N}$), each a commutative ring and a cocommutative Hopf algebra over $k$ that is finite and free as a $k$-module with $\operatorname{rank}_k A_v = p^{vh}$, together with surjective morphisms `G.transition v` $: A_{v+1} \to A_v$ of Hopf algebras whose kernel is the ideal generated by the image of the augmentation ideal $\ker(\varepsilon_{A_{v+1}})$ under the multiplication-by-$p^v$ map `nsmulAlgHom`. Write $A_1 =$ `G.level 1`. Let $x \in A_1$ be such that for every element $\varphi$ of [`CartierDual k (G.level 1)`](def/HopfAlgebra_CartierDual.html#L12), that is every $k$-linear functional $\varphi \colon A_1 \to k$, the $p$-th power $\varphi^p$ formed in the ring structure of the Cartier dual satisfies $\varphi^p(x) = 0$. The conclusion is that $x$ belongs to the ideal of $A_1$ generated by the set $\{a^p : a \in \ker(\varepsilon_{A_1})\}$, the image of the augmentation ideal `augIdeal k (G.level 1)` under the $p$-th power map.
--
--   In classical terms this is the inclusion $\ker F \subseteq \operatorname{im} V$ for the Frobenius and Verschiebung of $G[p]$: the ideal generated by $p$-th powers of augmentation-ideal elements cuts out $\ker F$, while the functionals killing $x$ after $p$-th convolution power detect the scheme-theoretic image of $V$. It is used in the proof that the dimension of $G$ and that of its Cartier dual add up to the height $h$, via [`PDivisibleGroup.CartierDuality.finrank_cotangent_one_add_finrank_cotangent_one_eq_height`](thm.html#PDivisibleGroup.CartierDuality.finrank_cotangent_one_add_finrank_cotangent_one_eq_height).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PDivisibleGroup_mem_span_pow_of_forall_pow_apply_eq_zero.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_PDivisibleGroup_Basic
import Definitions.Def_HopfAlgebra_CartierDual

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
